{{Codex|The Miter launches high velocity saw blades, tearing apart anyone unfortunate enough to be in their path.}}

The '''Miter''' is a saw blade launcher used by {{Faction|Grineer}} [[Eviscerator]]s. The disc must be charged in order to deal maximum damage. However, weaker uncharged shots can be fired in rapid succession as well.

This weapon is a [[weapon crafting ingredient]] for {{Weapon|Panthera}}.
{{Checklist|nocategory=true|
* {{Weapon|Miter}} + {{Weapon|Hikou}} → {{Weapon|Panthera}}
}}

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Slash}} damage.
*Charged shots have innate 2.5 meter [[punch through]].
*Innate {{Pol|Naramon}} polarity.
*Can equip the Miter-exclusive {{M|Neutralizing Justice}} mod.

{{Advantages|class=Bow|
*Highest [[status chance]] of all charged rifles.
*No [[recoil]] and pinpoint [[accuracy]].
*Shots [[ricochet]] off surfaces, up to five times, allowing them to hit multiple targets or hit the same target.
*Wide projectiles with 0.2m radius, allowing them to hit multiple targets standing next to each-other.
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Bow|
*Projectiles have slow travel time.
}}

{{Acquisition|Miter's main blueprint and components can be obtained from the dual boss team [[Lieutenant Lech Kril|Lech Kril]] and [[Captain Vor]] on [[Exta]], [[Ceres]].}}
{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}
This weapon can be sold for {{cc|7,500}}.

== Incarnon Genesis ==
{{Transclude|Miter Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Miter Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*The Miter has a high chance of cutting corpses into pieces, making it an ideal candidate for a [[Desecrate|Desecrating]] {{WF|Nekros}} to bring along, as the game considers the cut corpses as separate entities, essentially giving multiple corpses to desecrate from a single enemy and thus yielding more chances to create more drops.
*Fully charged rounds have high [[punch through]], making it effective against large groups, particularly [[Infested]] due to the high {{D|Slash}} damage.
**This also makes it possible to hit a single enemy twice with one shot: shooting a charged round directly at an enemy in front of a wall will make the rebounded blade hit the enemy a second time.
*Mods that affect fire rate also affect the [[Fire Rate#Charged Weapons|charging time]].
*Using [[Squad Ammo Restore]]s or {{Companion|Carrier}}'s {{M|Ammo Case}} is highly recommended as ammo can drain fast with normal attacks.
*As the weapon's projectiles start their flight at the rear of the weapon (compared to the edge of the barrel for most weapons) and fly in straight lines, it is not recommended to use {{M|Heavy Caliber}} as the mod will cause the blades to be fired at wide angles from the aiming reticle at high ranks.
*While having a crit chance of only 5% on uncharged shots, fully charged shots have a base crit chance of 10% which is enough to bring it up to 25% with {{M|Point Strike}}, enough to take advantage of heavy critical headshot slash procs that are very common with the Miter due to having mostly slash damage.
**With the addition of the crits on charged shots, it's possible to deal high damage {{D|Slash}} status effects when landing a critical hit and a status proc on a headshot on an enemy. This allows the weapon to perform surprisingly well on higher levels, similar to how the {{Weapon|Dread}} can cause strong {{D|Slash}} procs even through heavy grineer armor.
**It can be useful to add {{M|Continuous Misery}} to the weapon to extend the {{D|Slash}} proc's duration.
*Due to the slow projectile speed, it can be difficult to hit targets, even if they are directly approaching you. If you instead aim at the ground ahead of them, the blade will ricochet off of the ground and will be more likely to hit your target.

==Bugs ==
*The Incarnon Evolution III perk '''Ready Retaliation''' does not work, granting no reload speed.
*When fired from a hologram via {{A|Hall of Mirrors}}, the projectile will be the user's color palette, however the destroyed sawblade will be the default palette upon contact with a second bounce.
*When firing the projectiles at a Button on certain Orokin missions, the blades will hit the button and spin in place. At the end of their flight time, they will fall to the ground.
*With [[incarnon adapter]] installed, arsenal only displays stats for the incarnon form.

==Trivia== 
*The Miter has a non-static model; its discs rotate inside the weapon during charging, although the effect is barely visible to the user due to the position of the gun.
*The Miter was first seen in the game with the Grineer [[Eviscerator]] in the [[Sling-Stone Event]].
*Written on the disc is the word {{GrineerScript|CUTFACE}} which translates to "Cutface" in Grineer.
*The Miter can be carried by [[Grineer Target]]s in a [[Capture]] mission.
*A blade that has been shot can be found on the ground shortly after its third impact. After a few seconds it will disappear.
*Reloading, even while the magazine is empty, will always eject a saw out the top of the magazine that uses the default colors, remaining intact. This is unlike fired blades which retain customization colors but crumple when they bounce and drop to the floor.
*When held using {{A|Hall of Mirrors}}, the sawblade will not be hidden if the player looks through one of their clones.
*[[Grineer]] [[Eviscerator]]s seem to be able to fire the weapon faster than a player can without any [[fire rate]] [[Mod]]s (uncharged).
*The {{Weapon|Panthera}}, a rifle which requires the Miter as a prerequisite to be built, similarly fires sawblades, with an additional ability to fire a levitating saw that deals continuous damage.
**Slightly contrasting the Miter, however, the Panthera's sawblades are aligned vertically, compared to the Miter, whose sawblades are aligned horizontally.
** It cannot charge its attacks unlike the Miter.
*The Miter can be considered among the toughest weapons to acquire, due to its high number of parts in addition to the {{Weapon|Twin Gremlins}} Blueprint being on the same drop table, it's highly likely to end up with multiple duplicates before getting the last required part.
* Up until the introduction of the {{Weapon|Shedu}}, the Miter was the only weapon to use a Chassis as a component.
*The name "Miter" could be derived from a [[wikipedia:Miter saw|miter saw]], a type of power saw with a circular sawblade, and/or from the Latin word [[wiktionary:mittere|mittere]] (mitto), which means to throw.

