The '''Mk1-Kunai''' is [[Mk1]] variant of the {{Weapon|Kunai}} and is the standard issue throwing knives for all [[Tenno]] recruit, suited for new players who desire a silent and stealthy sidearm.

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|2,500}}.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Innate two {{Pol|Madurai}} polarities.

{{Advantages|
*[[Silent]].
}}

{{Disadvantages|.
*Projectiles have travel time with arcing.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Kunai}}

==Acquisition==
Mk1-Kunai can be purchased from the [[Market]] for {{cc|15,000}}.

==Notes==
*The Mk1-Kunai does not have the pinning properties of other projectile weapons, such as the {{Weapon|Boltor}} or {{Weapon|Paris}}, but will simply throw targets backwards upon death.

==Incarnon Genesis==
{{Transclude|Kunai Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Kunai Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*Make sure to adjust your aim for moving targets.
*When using at a distance, aim above the enemy to adjust for the arc of the blades.
*Using the {{M|Pistol Ammo Mutation}} mod can help regain lost ammo when needed.
**Alternatively, bring along [[Squad Ammo Restore]]s.

==Trivia==
*The Kunai (苦無) was traditionally a multipurpose tool, similar in design to a crowbar. It could be used for gardening, masonry, and other things.
*In popular culture, the word "Kunai" is often associated with ninjas and is depicted as a throwing knife.
*The Mk1-Kunai was introduced as a new starting weapon option in {{ver|14}}, alongside the {{Weapon|Lato}} and the {{Weapon|Mk1-Furis}}.
*The Mk1-Kunai is the only weapon obtainable in Vor's Prize yet to receive a [[prime]] upgrade.
**The {{Weapon|Spira Prime}} was originally meant to be the Prime upgrade to the Kunai, but it was mistranslated to Spira, DE changed its stats and made it the Prime to the normal {{Weapon|Spira}} .

==Bugs==
*Despite being acquirable from the [[Vor's Prize]] tutorial, the Mk1-Kunai currently requires [[Mastery Rank]] 2 to purchase.

